<!--
  Charge (2026-11): navigate to a staging pose in front of the charger with
  move.xml's machinery, switch the gait to MPC and let it settle, then look
  for the charger's tag and walk the last metre onto the charger on the tag
  itself -- TrackPose following the sightings PublishLandmark publishes --
  and lie down there, on the contacts.

  Selected per goal by NavigateToGoal.behavior_tree ("charge.xml"). Until
  2026-11-12 dock.xml sat beside it, and its header (git history) is the
  design record for what the two shared: the staging leg (move.xml with
  goal="{staging_pose}"), the overlay clear, the MPC switch and its check
  (SetMotionKey 5 -> WaitForMotionState 5 -> Wait 3000), RL restored only on
  a failure after the switch was attempted, no in-tree retry of the
  approach, the attribution and the status sentences. What is different
  here, and why:

  The goal's `pose` is the TAG, not where the robot ends: the charger's
  marker in the map, its yaw pointing out of its face (what the console's
  Charger waypoint stores from its Detect button). The map pose is only good
  enough to get in front of the charger. ComputeStagingPose facing_landmark
  puts the staging pose `distance` out along that yaw, turned to face the
  tag: 1.3 m, where the tag fills enough of the image for a pose and the
  robot has 0.76 m to walk in.

  Why not dock.xml with the tag's pose: DockToPose drives to a pose fixed in
  odom at acceptance, so it ends wherever the map said the charger was -- off
  by the localizer's error and the waypoint's, centimetres either way, on
  contacts that take about three. TrackPose (syncai_common/TrackPose,
  controller_server) drives to where the TAG is seen to be, corrected by
  every sighting, with the Charging controller (ApproachController), which
  strafes: a charger's tolerance is across its axis, and Docking's law only
  walks forward and turns.

  Detection starts only once the gait has switched and settled (2026-11-12,
  on request; it ran before the switch until then): DetectLandmark waits up
  to 5 s for the first trusted sighting of the tag, standing in MPC, then
  the approach starts. It also wakes the detector, which sleeps until polled
  (its first answers are SENSOR_STARTING). Inside the MPC half, so a tag not
  in view is DOCK_FAILED with the detector's last word AND RL restored -- the
  price of the order is an MPC switch for nothing when the tag cannot be
  seen from the staging pose.

  The last metre is a Parallel of two nodes, because the detector publishes
  nothing by itself and the controller judges nothing:
   - PublishLandmark polls detect_landmark and publishes the sightings it
     TRUSTS on tracked_landmark -- at least 3 sightings in a row. It never
     succeeds;
     it fails only when detection cannot work at all (unknown landmark, the
     detector silent or SENSOR_UNAVAILABLE for 5 s). A tag out of view is
     not its failure: nothing is published, and TrackPose's pose_timeout
     (stop) and lost_timeout (LOST) judge that.
   - TrackPose follows that topic. Its success ends the Parallel
     (success_threshold 1) and halts the publisher; either one failing
     fails it (failure_threshold 1), which cancels the approach.
  ambiguous="ignore_orientation" on both detection nodes (2026-11-18): from the
  staging pose every sighting is ambiguous -- ArUco's two mirrored solutions
  only merge within about 0.6 m of the tag -- so the default, "drop", never
  found the tag, and using them as given had the target jump between the two solutions
  and the robot stop 76 times in 85 s without advancing. ignore_orientation keeps
  an ambiguous sighting's position and turns its face square to the camera;
  inside 0.6 m the sightings are not ambiguous and are sent as given.
  Replayed on that day's bags, a full pose from beyond 0.65 m put the target
  4-5 cm off the tag's axis whichever solution was picked and the position
  alone 2.4 cm, which is why there is no switch back to the full pose nearer in.

  THE CHARGER'S GEOMETRY IS THE TrackPose offset AND NOWHERE ELSE: offset_x
  is where base_link stands on the charger, metres out from the tag along
  its face normal, and offset_yaw pi turns the robot to face it. 0.50 since
  2026-11-18: at 0.54 robot01 lay 0.043 m short of the contacts and was
  pushed onto them by hand (one run, read off the odometry; from the stop to
  lying still the body also moved 0.04 m back, which this does not undo by
  itself if it varies). Before that, 0.54 =
  SyncAI-Robot-Charger's stop, 0.27 m from the tag at the CAMERA, plus the
  camera's 0.27 m ahead of base_link (G23.urdf). Derived, not measured: lay
  the robot on the charger and read the tag's distance in base_link. The
  Charging controller's view_distance (controller_server_params.yaml) must
  equal it -- that is the point the nose is held on, the tag.

  filter_window 1.0: track_pose drives to the median of the last second of
  sightings (taken into odom, where a charger stands still), because one
  sighting's yaw noise moves the target centimetres across its axis; the
  same window is its test that the odometry is holding still. The server
  freezes the target once the robot is inside the goal checker's
  tolerances, where the tag may leave the image.

  The tree LIES THE ROBOT DOWN on the charger (2026-11-12, on request):
  after TrackPose succeeds, a Wait of 2000 ms standing still (2026-11-18:
  the goal check accepts a position, and the gait is still stepping when it
  does), then SetMotionKey key="2" (`MODE X`) and a Wait of
  4000 ms, so SUCCEEDED means "lying on the charger". dock.xml did the same
  from 2026-10-14 to 2026-10-15 and dropped it for the backend's LIEDOWN
  step; a charge needs the contacts loaded, so here it is part of the step.
  There is no report of a lie-down to wait for (WaitForMotionState knows
  MPC = 5 and RL = 1 only), so the 4000 ms is dock.xml's guess, not a
  measurement. It sits AFTER the MPC half's Fallback: a refused lie-down
  fails the goal (DOCK_FAILED, SetMotionKey's reason) but does not send RL,
  which would start the locomotion policy on the contacts -- the robot is
  left standing on the charger in MPC.

  Nothing leaves the charger since undock.xml went (2026-11-12): a robot
  lying on it has to be stood up (STANDUP) and backed off by the caller.

  A preempt that moves {goal} after the staging leg reaches neither node:
  TrackPose's goal has no pose in it, and the tag in view is the one driven
  to. Send a moved charger once this goal has ended.
-->
<root main_tree_to_execute="MainTree">
  <BehaviorTree ID="MainTree">
    <Sequence name="Charge">
      <!-- New goal, clean obstacle memory: move.xml's first node (see dock.xml's header) -->
      <ForceSuccess>
        <ClearEntireCostmap name="ClearDynamicOverlay-NewGoal" service_name="planner_server/Octo3D/clear_overlay" server_timeout="1000"/>
      </ForceSuccess>
      <!-- Staging leg: move.xml with goal="{staging_pose}"; see move.xml for the why -->
      <PipelineSequence name="NavigateToStaging">
        <RateController hz="1.0">
          <RecoveryNode number_of_retries="1" name="ComputePathToPose">
            <Fallback name="FallbackComputePathToPose">
              <ReactiveSequence name="CheckIfNewPathNeeded">
                <Inverter>
                  <GlobalUpdatedGoal/>
                </Inverter>
                <!-- Judged by Octo3D on its dynamic overlay (see move.xml) -->
                <IsPathValid path="{path}" server_timeout="100" blocked_time="10.0"/>
              </ReactiveSequence>
              <Sequence name="PlanToStaging">
                <!-- {goal} is the charger's tag: stage in front of it, facing it -->
                <ComputeStagingPose dock_pose="{goal}" distance="1.3" facing_landmark="true" staging_pose="{staging_pose}"/>
                <ComputePathToPose goal="{staging_pose}" path="{path}" planner_id="Octo3D"/>
              </Sequence>
            </Fallback>
            <ForceSuccess>
              <ClearEntireCostmap name="ClearDynamicOverlay-Context" service_name="planner_server/Octo3D/clear_overlay"/>
            </ForceSuccess>
          </RecoveryNode>
        </RateController>
        <RecoveryNode number_of_retries="4" retry_refill_time="60.0" name="FollowPath">
          <FollowPath path="{path}" controller_id="FollowPath"/>
          <ForceSuccess>
            <ClearEntireCostmap name="ClearLocalCostmap-Context" service_name="local_costmap/clear_entirely_local_costmap"/>
          </ForceSuccess>
        </RecoveryNode>
      </PipelineSequence>

      <!-- MPC half: restore RL on any failure after the switch was attempted -->
      <Fallback name="ChargeInMpc">
        <Sequence name="SwitchAndApproach">
          <SetBlackboard output_key="nav_status_msg" value="Switching the gait to MPC for charging"/>
          <SetMotionKey key="5" server_timeout="500"/>
          <!-- Confirm the controller reports MPC (mode data[1] == 5), then let it settle (dock.xml) -->
          <WaitForMotionState state="5" timeout="5000"/>
          <Wait msec="3000"/>
          <!-- Only now look for the tag (header): standing still in MPC -->
          <SetBlackboard output_key="nav_status_msg" value="Looking for the charger's marker"/>
          <DetectLandmark landmark_id="charger_a" min_consecutive="3" timeout="5000" ambiguous="ignore_orientation"/>
          <Parallel name="ApproachOnTheTag" success_threshold="1" failure_threshold="1">
            <PublishLandmark landmark_id="charger_a" min_consecutive="3" topic="tracked_landmark" sensor_timeout="5000" ambiguous="ignore_orientation"/>
            <TrackPose pose_topic="tracked_landmark" offset_x="0.50" offset_y="0.0" offset_yaw="3.141592653589793" controller_id="Charging" goal_checker_id="charge_goal_checker" filter_window="1.0"/>
          </Parallel>
        </Sequence>
        <ForceFailure>
          <SetMotionKey name="RestoreRL" key="1" server_timeout="500"/>
        </ForceFailure>
      </Fallback>

      <!-- On the charger: lie down on the contacts (header). After the
           Fallback on purpose -- a refused lie-down must not send RL -->
      <Sequence name="LieDownOnCharger">
        <SetBlackboard output_key="nav_status_msg" value="On the charger, standing still before lying down"/>
        <!-- Stand 2 s first (2026-11-18, on request): track_pose's goal check
             is a position held inside its tolerances, not a body at rest. On
             robot01 that day it succeeded 0.45 s after a reverse command, and
             the lie-down went out 0.15 s later with the gait still stepping -->
        <Wait name="StandStillOnCharger" msec="2000"/>
        <SetBlackboard output_key="nav_status_msg" value="Lying down on the charger"/>
        <SetMotionKey name="LieDown" key="2" server_timeout="500"/>
        <Wait msec="4000"/>
      </Sequence>
    </Sequence>
  </BehaviorTree>
</root>
